        "original_id": "19f26664-dcbb-5171-afe9-48881f8a5211",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Is Anybody Out There?, singles, LP records, albums, EP records\n- Systems: Canadian Hot 100\n- Companies: Billboard\n- Places: Canada\n- Concepts: music industry record charts, music releases\n\nFacts:\n- The Canadian Hot 100 is a weekly singles music industry record chart in Canada.\n- Billboard magazine publishes the Canadian Hot 100.\n- A single, record single, or music single is a music release that typically contains fewer tracks than an LP record, album, or EP record.\n- A single is usually released separately from an album, although it often also appears on an album.\n- The single \"Is Anybody Out There?\" debuted at number 67 on the Canadian Hot 100 and later peaked at number 14.",
